  "summary": "Four series priced separately on one page, and each is listed here under its own name: Nova single-GPU VMs with NVLink, the Atlas and Yotta pods, and the Orion nodes, whose eight-GPU bare-metal machines are the cheapest way this provider sells an H200 or an RTX PRO 6000. vCPU and memory are included in every rate; storage is billed on top. Nova's spot rate is for capacity that may be reclaimed when demand rises. The page draws three of its four price tables from files it loads itself, and prints \"Getting Real Time Cost...\" while one of them is unavailable.",
  "notes": "Four books on one page, each published as its own series in the region column; the figure recorded is the two-decimal one the page prints; Nova spot is exactly half its on-demand rate (the provider's own rule); the X-Series prices no card and the marketplace is behind a login, so neither is read; a book that does not answer is skipped rather than failing the provider",
